    {
      "id": "claim_071080a283b44edf8ea3b24209727a22",
      "statement": "addBreachCompensation refuses a requestRef that is not an evidence.fulfillment_request, then emits bind-breach-rule first — a breach rule named rule.<requestRef>-breached whose description is the intent's business condition, binding the request, the confirmations alias and now, with expression `now > request.expired_at && !confirmations.exists(c, c.confirmed_at <= request.expired_at)` — followed by the ordinary fulfillment-pair commands in the breached request's Contract Context, so a missed deadline becomes a new pair plus a rule and never a rollback or retry of the original pair.",
